# UGE GitHub repo standard

When the user asks for a **new hardware repo**, **new module repo**, **new library repo**, or **UGE product repo**, follow this layout.

## Repo types

**Hardware/module:** `README.md`, `IMGs/`, `site/`, `.github/workflows/pages.yml`, optional BOM/schematic in repo root or `docs/`.

**Arduino library:** add `examples/` with `Basics/`, `Network/`, `TCP/`, `UDP/`, `Advanced/` and `examples/README.md` (table of sketches).

## Required files

```
site/index.html       # branded landing page (copy from repo-template)
site/.nojekyll        # required for raw HTML (interactive BOM)
.github/workflows/pages.yml
.cursor/rules/uge-github-repos.mdc
```

## Pages workflow

- Source: **GitHub Actions** (not branch deploy).
- Build step copies `site/*` plus every asset referenced in `index.html` into `_site/`.
- First deploy: remind user to enable **Settings → Pages → GitHub Actions** if workflow fails.

## README section order (hardware)

1. Title + hero from `IMGs/`
2. Buy options (assembled + DIY PCB → uge-one.com)
3. Key features
4. Specs / wiring tables
5. Library & firmware links
6. Examples
7. Repo layout

## Brand defaults

- Org: `https://github.com/UGEelectronics/<repo>`
- Store: `https://uge-one.com`
- Pages URL: `https://ugeelectronics.github.io/<repo>/`
- Footer: "UG Electronics · uge-one.com"

## Reference

Use [CH390H-SPI-EthernetController](https://github.com/UGEelectronics/CH390H-SPI-EthernetController) or the org template `UGEelectronics/repo-template` when scaffolding.

